<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  RM_FlamefangVenomBite.xml            Pyrelands — FLAMEFANG_SNAKE_REBIRTH_1

  Delivery half of the venom mechanism — see HediffDefs/RM_FlamefangVenom.xml
  for the full citation of the vanilla pattern this copies (Cobra's ToxicBite
  DamageDef, RimSage-verified: ParentName="Bite" + <additionalHediffs>
  injecting a HediffDef scaled by <severityPerDamageDealt>). ParentName="Bite"
  is a real, Name-attributed vanilla DamageDef (Defs/Core/DamageDefs/
  Damages_MeleeWeapon.xml) so this inherits armorCategory/hediff/
  hediffSolid/impactSoundType/workerClass etc. from it unchanged; only the
  label and the venom injection are new.

  Dose: 0.009 severity per point of damage, scaled by inverse body size like
  vanilla ToxicBite. The fauna normalization (RimUtinni
  FaunaNorm_Law3_Damage.xml) sets the venom-fangs' power to 22.5, so a bite on
  a human lands ~0.2 (0.16..0.24 with vanilla's 0.8..1.2 damage roll). At the
  old 0.02 that patch made the dose 0.45, and one untended bite killed before
  immunity (Pyrelands visit 3, 2026-11-21). The one-bite course, with the
  immunity rate in HediffDefs/RM_FlamefangVenom.xml, is tested by
  selftest_pyrelands_venom_dose.py, which reads the power after the patch.

  Reached from RM_Flamefang's own bite tool
  (Defs/ThingDefs_Races/RM_PyrelandsPortedFauna.xml) through the matching
  ToolCapacityDefs/RM_FlamefangBite.xml capacity + maneuver pair (mirrors
  GeneticRim's own GR_VeryToxicBite capacity/maneuver/damage trio, which the
  donor def this creature was ported off used).
-->
<Defs>

  <DamageDef ParentName="Bite">
    <defName>RM_FlamefangVenomBite</defName>
    <label>venomous bite</label>
    <additionalHediffs>
      <li>
        <hediff>RM_FlamefangVenom</hediff>
        <severityPerDamageDealt>0.009</severityPerDamageDealt>
        <victimSeverityScalingByInvBodySize>true</victimSeverityScalingByInvBodySize>
      </li>
    </additionalHediffs>
    <applyAdditionalHediffsIfHuntingForFood>false</applyAdditionalHediffsIfHuntingForFood>
    <damageEffecter>Impact_Toxic</damageEffecter>
  </DamageDef>

</Defs>
